ClaudeDock — Third-Party Acknowledgments & Inspirations
=======================================================

ClaudeDock is an independent, clean-room native Swift/SwiftUI macOS application
and CLI. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Anthropic, PBC.
"Claude" and "Claude Desktop" are trademarks of Anthropic, PBC.

ClaudeDock builds upon ideas pioneered by the open-source community:

1. claude-multi-desktop (MIT License)
   https://github.com/jackson-cmd/claude-multi-desktop
   Inspiration: zero-patch macOS Claude.app multi-instance launchers via
   Electron's `--user-data-dir`, dynamic badged launcher icons, shared
   `~/.claude` configuration, and cross-account Claude Code peer discovery.

2. Claude-Cage (MIT License)
   https://github.com/Lee-xeo/Claude-Cage
   Inspiration: zero-token quota probing via Claude CLI `control_request:
   get_usage`, three-way configuration synchronization with backups, passive
   account identity observation, and fail-closed egress/region discipline.

All source code in ClaudeDock is written from scratch in Swift 6 using native
Apple frameworks (Foundation, AppKit, SwiftUI, Carbon, ServiceManagement) with
zero external package dependencies.
